<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ accommodation occupancy low in August - SNZ.</title>
<headline>NZ accommodation occupancy low in August - SNZ.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand accommodation occupancy remained low in August 1996 at 27 percent, Statistics New Zealand said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Hotels had an occupancy rate of 49 percent, motels 45 percent and backpackers/hostels 38 percent.</p>
<p>The survey covered accommodation providers throughout New Zealand.</p>
<p>The Wellington region had the highest occupancy rate at 49 percent and Auckland was second with 48 percent occupancy. The lowest occupancy rate was 14 percent recorded in Northland.  </p>
<p>The average length of stay by guests in all accommodation establishments in August was 2.1 nights, SNZ said.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
